  "id": "flow",
  "term": "flow",
  "definition": "Flow is an optimal mental state in which a person becomes deeply absorbed in an activity, with intense focus, enjoyment, a sense of control, and less self-consciousness. It happens when someone is fully engaged in what they are doing, though it can be a fragile state that depends on how attention, action, and emotion are managed.",
